{"content":[{"c":["JOHN (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Father of Simon Peter and Andrew (",{"href":"?bref=John.1.40-42","r":"John.1.40-42","rawR":"John.1.40-42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.40-42","value":"John.1.40-42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 1:40-42"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.21.15-17","r":"John.21.15-17","rawR":"John.21.15-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.21.15-17","value":"John.21.15-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:15-17"},"). According to ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.16.17","r":"Matt.16.17","rawR":"Matt.16.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.16.17","value":"Matt.16.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matthew 16:17"},", Peter’s father was named Jona (Jonas, Jonah). Either Jona was an alternate form of the name John or, more probably, two independent traditions existed regarding his name."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Member of the high priestly family who, along with Annas, Caiaphas, and Alexander, questioned Peter and John after the two apostles had healed a lame man (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.4.6","r":"Acts.4.6","rawR":"Acts.4.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.4.6","value":"Acts.4.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 4:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. According to the early church bishop Papias, a member of the larger group of Jesus’ disciples outside the Twelve (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.10.1","r":"Luke.10.1","rawR":"Luke.10.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.10.1","value":"Luke.10.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 10:1"},"). Known as “John the elder” (the presbyter), he is often credited with the authorship of 2 and 3 John (",{"href":"?bref=2Jn.1.1","r":"2Jn.1.1","rawR":"2Jn.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Jn.1.1","value":"2Jn.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Jn 1:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=3Jn.1.1","r":"3Jn.1.1","rawR":"3Jn.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"3Jn.1.1","value":"3Jn.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"3 Jn 1:1"},"), although the term “elder” there more likely refers to John the apostle."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. The apostle. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JohntheApostle_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JohntheApostle_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JohntheApostle_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"John, The Apostle"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. The Baptist. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JohntheBaptist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JohntheBaptist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JohntheBaptist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"John the Baptist"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. An early disciple known as John Mark, author of the second Gospel. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MarkJohn_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MarkJohn_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MarkJohn_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mark, John"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"JohnPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jn 1:40-42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.1.40-42","rawQueryValue":"John.1.40-42","sourceRefExact":"John.1.40-42"},{"anchorText":"21:15-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.21.15-17","rawQueryValue":"John.21.15-17","sourceRefExact":"John.21.15-17"},{"anchorText":"Matthew 16:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.16.17","rawQueryValue":"Matt.16.17","sourceRefExact":"Matt.16.17"},{"anchorText":"Acts 4:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.4.6","rawQueryValue":"Acts.4.6","sourceRefExact":"Acts.4.6"},{"anchorText":"Lk 10:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.10.1","rawQueryValue":"Luke.10.1","sourceRefExact":"Luke.10.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Jn 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Jn.1.1","rawQueryValue":"2Jn.1.1","sourceRefExact":"2Jn.1.1"},{"anchorText":"3 Jn 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=3Jn.1.1","rawQueryValue":"3Jn.1.1","sourceRefExact":"3Jn.1.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0a8b57614d7eb24efec133f8888195fb47750e5a509b5804fa551e3d054f0184","sourceItemName":"JohnPerson","sourceItemOrder":279,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"JohnPerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"John (Person)","title":"John (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}